  "claim": "Across 40 crashes injected at every phase of a write, programs resumed on another node with no repeated writes (the 95% upper bound on the duplicate rate is 7.5%). The median resume took about 12 seconds, set by the lease timeout. Writes caught mid-flight are marked outcome unknown for a person to resolve. Under these settings, 0.0% of surviving nodes paused themselves for safety, and 0.0% of resumes missed the recovery deadline.",
  "honesty": "Two celld nodes, one object-storage provider (R2). Not durable execution / exactly-once. Columns: duplicates (safety), outcome_unknown (uncertainty), survivor self-fence/restart (availability), claim-path completed + stepsRepeated, plus statePreserved (structural baseline pairing on outer phases) and waitApproval (FLEET_PHASED_AWAIT_TRIALS arm). Aggregate outcome_unknown ≈ half only because kills are aimed evenly at four phases — two are the in-flight window; outer phases must stay 0 (nonzero = bug). Real crashes mostly miss that brief window. Resume p50 ≈ lease TTL + detection (failover floor); raising TTL alone slows every crash. Preferred levers (planned, not measured): renew more often within the same TTL, regional lease store — see AVAILABILITY.md / TTL-TRADEOFF.md.",
